      <div class="case-cell room-bedroom"></div>
      <div class="case-cell room-bedroom"></div>
      <div class="case-cell room-library"></div>
      <div class="case-cell room-bedroom"></div>
      <div class="case-cell room-bedroom"></div>
      <div class="case-cell room-bedroom cell-rug"></div>
      <div class="case-cell room-bedroom"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="board-caption">The case board: victim V in the Kitchen, three cats unaccounted for.</p>

    <h3>Step 1: Let the Sudoku Rule Do the Heavy Lifting</h3>

    <p><span class="step-tag">1</span>V sits in row 1, column 2, so no suspect can use row 1 or column 2. That confines Mochi, Tofu, and Pixel to rows 2, 3, and 4, in columns 1, 3, and 4. Three suspects, three rows, three columns: the board is already half-solved before you have read a single statement.</p>

    <h3>Step 2: Mochi's Statement Resolves to One Cell</h3>

    <p><span class="step-tag">2</span>Mochi was in the Kitchen. The Kitchen covers the top-left 2×2 block, but row 1 is off limits (the victim's row) and column 2 is off limits (the victim's column). Cross out (r1c1), (r1c2), and (r2c2), and exactly one Kitchen cell survives: <strong>(r2c1)</strong>. Mochi's position is forced, no guessing required.</p>

    <h3>Step 3: Tofu's Statement Resolves to One Cell</h3>

    <p><span class="step-tag">3</span>Tofu was in the Library, the L-shaped room along the top right. Its cells are (r1c3), (r1c4), (r2c3), (r2c4), and (r3c4). Row 1 is taken by the victim, and row 2 is taken by Mochi, so four of the five cells drop away: <strong>(r3c4)</strong> is the only Library cell left. Tofu is forced too.</p>

    <h3>Step 4: Pixel Falls Out of the Grid Itself</h3>

    <p><span class="step-tag">4</span>One row (4) and one column (3) remain, so Pixel must stand at <strong>(r4c3)</strong>. Check the statement: the rug is exactly there, so Pixel's alibi checks out. In easy cases like this one, the last suspect often falls out of the grid automatically, and their clue serves as confirmation rather than elimination.</p>

    <div class="case-board" role="img" aria-label="The solved case grid. Mochi M stands in the kitchen at row 2 column 1, highlighted as the killer. Tofu T stands in the library at row 3 column 4. Pixel P stands on the rug in the bedroom at row 4 column 3. The victim V remains in the kitchen.">
      <div class="case-cell room-kitchen"><span class="room-label">Kitchen</span></div>
      <div class="case-cell room-kitchen cell-victim">V</div>
      <div class="case-cell room-library"><span class="room-label">Library</span></div>
